# BEGIN VIVO DOCKER-USER
# Docker-published ports (go2rtc 1984/8554/8555, Frigate 8971) bypass ufw's
# INPUT rules, so they are filtered here: only the allowed networks get in.
# Managed by gateway/setup.sh; edit site.env (LAN_CIDRS, ADMIN_CIDRS, WEBRTC_PUBLIC) instead.
# WEBRTC_PUBLIC=1 opens only UDP 8555 (go2rtc WebRTC) to everyone, for direct remote live view;
# ICE answers only peers that know the session's credentials. What stays exposed is go2rtc's
# STUN/DTLS handling on that one port, rate limited per source address (200 packets a second).
*filter
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i docker0 -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i br-+ -j RETURN
@ALLOWED_NETWORKS@
@PUBLIC_WEBRTC@
-A DOCKER-USER -j DROP
COMMIT
# END VIVO DOCKER-USER
